  "body": "## What changed\n\nRoot cause: `wcs_pick::arm` leaves the toolbar's pick mode alone on purpose, because the row takes faces, edges and corners together. But `interact::pick_at` sent a viewport click to `feature_click::click` only when `geo_pick` was Face, Edge or Vertex, and `update_hover` had the same gate. The default mode is Model, and the only control that changes it is on an operation's Geometry page. So from a fresh project every click selected the whole model and the armed draft never received a pick. `feature_click::ask` and `click` already handled the armed row; they were just never reached.\n\nFix: a new predicate, `interact::feature_routed`, is true in a feature mode or while `wcs_pick::collecting`. Both the click and the hover route on it. Disarmed or paused, the mode's own click behaviour is back. Apply is unchanged: it still queues the undoable `SetWcs`, whose MCP tool is untouched. A tilted frame is still placed, and generation still refuses it by name (#1518). The other setup drafts (plane, points, axis, locate, boundary) switch the mode when armed, so they did not have this gap.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/1562-wcs-pick-route.md` (route on the draft's state rather than switching the mode and restoring it on every exit path).\n\n## How tested\n\n- Pinning test: `egui_app::wcs_pick_click_tests::an_armed_row_takes_viewport_picks_from_the_default_model_mode` (ui lib). From a fresh project (mode Model, no operation open) it arms the row through its button, checks the hover names the top face, and drives a face (Z), an edge (X) and a corner (Origin) through `interact::pick_at`, never through `wcs_pick::take`. It checks that no whole-model Select is queued and that the \"Picked:\" line shows. It then clicks Apply, checks the WCS lands on the corner, and checks that a click after the draft ends is a whole-model select again.\n- Mutation check: I removed `|| crate::wcs_pick::collecting(state)` from `feature_routed`, and the test failed at the hover assert (line 83). I then reverted only the click routing in `pick_at` (keeping the hover), and it failed at the Z-pick assert (line 87). Both were restored.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (ui lib + boundary, boundary_picks, edge_loop_pick, operations, sinker_setup, theme_files; 59 s).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- The existing `wcs_pick_tests` and `wcs_pick::tests` pass unchanged.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- **A GUI hand check by the maintainer is owed**: real mouse clicks and the drawn hover highlight in the live viewport (the test covers the hover state, not the pixels).\n- No structural assertions changed: the row's labels and widgets are the same. No snapshot PNG was touched.\n- `interact.rs` was already over 400 lines before this change (1794); this PR adds 12.\n\nChangelog: \"Pick for WCS\" on the Setups page now takes face, edge and corner picks from the viewport in the default pick mode, and the hover highlights them (#1562)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nfork synced at v0.19.0 (branch cut from upstream/main f402b368)\n\nFixes #1562\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
